- “Restricted Entities” means any individual or entity that meets any of the following conditions:
  1. a natural person who is a national of a Covered Jurisdiction, who holds permanent resident status in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region or the Macao Special Administrative Region, or who habitually resides in a Covered Jurisdiction;
  2. a legal person, unincorporated organization, or other entity that is incorporated or otherwise formed in a Covered Jurisdiction, or whose principal place of business or actual place of operations is in a Covered Jurisdiction;
  3. any entity of which more than 5 percent of the equity, voting rights, or beneficial interests is held, directly or indirectly in the aggregate, by one or more persons or entities described in item 1 or item 2 above, or that is actually controlled by any such person or entity;
  4. a government authority or public body of a Covered Jurisdiction, and any enterprise or organization directly or indirectly controlled by it.

